Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:05:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add hackathons scraping feature

- Hackathon model + migration (source/external_id dedupe, region,
  open_state, virtual/in-person, first_seen_at as the "published" proxy)
- hackathon_scraper.py: polite Devpost adapter -- descriptive User-Agent,
  MAX_RETRIES=3 w/ exponential backoff + jitter on timeouts/429/5xx,
  graceful skip (no retry) on 4xx client errors, TTL response cache,
  rate-limit delay between requests, searches "Africa" + "South Africa"
- hackathon_service.py: region + virtual/in-person filtering, excludes
  ended hackathons by default, always orders recent-first
- hackathons blueprint nested under /community/hackathons: HTML page +
  simple JSON API, both session-gated like the rest of community
- Hackathons tab added to the forum sidebar via a shared
  _forum_sidebar.html partial (forum.html and hackathons.html both use it)
- flask scrape-hackathons CLI command + weekly GitHub Actions workflow
  (Monday 06:00 UTC, manually triggerable)

Verified: app boots and registers the blueprint, normalize/upsert logic
checked against a live-captured Devpost record (HTML stripped from
prize_amount, region derivation, virtual/in-person split), dedupe is
idempotent on re-scrape, ended hackathons are excluded, region/mode
filters and recent-first ordering all pass, routes render and the
JSON API returns the expected payload. Retry/backoff path exercised
live via this sandbox's network restrictions (3 attempts then a clean
graceful give-up, no crash).

Not yet run: `flask db upgrade` against the real database -- do that
before deploying.

